1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:05,233
Got an Uber today, got in the car, first thing the guy says to me is like, do you mind if I talk to a friend?

2
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:11,186
And I'm a normal guy, right? So I said, of course.

3
00:00:11,186 --> 00:00:22,096
And thank you for considering me a friend.

4
00:00:22,096 --> 00:00:26,378
We had the best conversation.

5
00:00:26,378 --> 00:00:27,584
So good.

6
00:00:27,584 --> 00:00:32,128
He was speaking Urdu and I responded in English.

7
00:00:32,128 --> 00:00:35,545
It was a beautiful cultural exchange.

8
00:00:35,545 --> 00:00:37,727
He kept doing this.

9
00:00:37,727 --> 00:00:43,054
I'm like, that must be a cultural gesture.

10
00:00:43,054 --> 00:00:49,452
So I did this.

11
00:00:49,452 --> 00:00:52,165
But I'm good.

12
00:00:52,165 --> 00:00:53,330
I've been doing well.

13
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:55,229
I've been cooking a lot.

14
00:00:55,229 --> 00:00:56,247
So good.

15
00:00:56,247 --> 00:00:58,681
I learned to cook online, right?

16
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:03,885
But I think it's so special that recipes that used to be passed down from generation to generation.

17
00:01:03,885 --> 00:01:06,016
I think that's so special.

18
00:01:06,016 --> 00:01:13,108
So I got to tell my kids that my grandfather passed me down Jamie Oliver's superfood pasta.

19
00:01:13,108 --> 00:01:16,797
Tell them that Jamie Oliver's a province in China.

20
00:01:16,797 --> 00:01:19,715
We're from the Jamie people.

21
00:01:19,715 --> 00:01:23,413
I've been cooking, I've been eating at other people's houses.

22
00:01:23,413 --> 00:01:25,908
Diversify the portfolio, you know?

23
00:01:25,908 --> 00:01:32,997
I was at a friend's house eating dinner and he cooked this lamb shoulder and it took him two days to cook this lamb shoulder.

24
00:01:32,997 --> 00:01:35,167
And he was bragging about it.

25
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:37,923
I didn't even know that was something you could brag about.

26
00:01:37,923 --> 00:01:40,683
Like the amount of time it took you to prepare the meal.

27
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:47,559
But I found it to be quite a good excuse to serve my guests leftovers.

28
00:01:47,559 --> 00:01:53,704
I went, this is a 24-hour stir-fry.

29
00:01:53,704 --> 00:01:59,914
This pizza's been dry-aged for seven days.

30
00:01:59,914 --> 00:02:01,255
Good stuff.

31
00:02:01,255 --> 00:02:02,303
I love food.

32
00:02:02,303 --> 00:02:04,979
I am a foodie. Guilty.

33
00:02:04,979 --> 00:02:07,315
I love food. I love coffee as well.

34
00:02:07,315 --> 00:02:09,209
Big coffee head.

35
00:02:09,209 --> 00:02:12,614
A couple of fans of coffee. Nice.

36
00:02:12,614 --> 00:02:17,640
I love coffee but I reckon coffee culture's gone nuts.

37
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,272
You know what I mean?

38
00:02:18,272 --> 00:02:20,008
Like it's gone too far.

39
00:02:20,008 --> 00:02:22,140
Because there's coffee places everywhere.

40
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:25,308
Like I saw a coffee place in a rock climbing gym.

41
00:02:25,308 --> 00:02:28,216
I'm like surely that's too far.

42
00:02:28,216 --> 00:02:30,573
There's a coffee place at my local library.

43
00:02:30,573 --> 00:02:33,743
I saw a woman order a triple shot latte.

44
00:02:33,743 --> 00:02:37,974
I'm like what book are you trying to read?

45
00:02:37,974 --> 00:02:40,780
Must be pretty tough.

46
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:45,598
You know I was getting a coffee from my mechanics and um...

47
00:02:45,598 --> 00:02:49,242
Mechanics are like the last profession that there's no regular retail price.

48
00:02:49,242 --> 00:02:49,854
Right?

49
00:02:49,854 --> 00:02:53,460
Like there's no sign behind them telling you how much it's gonna cost.

50
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,767
You can't just google how much a service is.

51
00:02:55,767 --> 00:03:00,183
Right? It's just numbers swirling around in their minds.

52
00:03:00,183 --> 00:03:06,872
Only they know on any given day how much they're gonna fleece you.

53
00:03:06,872 --> 00:03:12,040
I don't know if you can tell this just by looking at me but I'm not a pushover.

54
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:16,158
That's not a funny bit.

55
00:03:16,158 --> 00:03:17,540
Got a great deal out of this guy.

56
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:22,575
Two tyres. $7,000.

57
00:03:22,575 --> 00:03:24,711
He did upsell me though.

58
00:03:24,711 --> 00:03:26,152
I reckon he upsold me.

59
00:03:26,152 --> 00:03:28,603
I don't think I needed the second tyre.

60
00:03:28,603 --> 00:03:32,305
I just went in for a latte.

61
00:03:32,305 --> 00:03:35,171
This mechanic, he kept saying the word roughly.

62
00:03:35,171 --> 00:03:38,083
Right? He's like it's roughly quite a big job.

63
00:03:38,083 --> 00:03:40,191
It's roughly gonna take one to two days.

64
00:03:40,191 --> 00:03:46,996
Like he kept saying the word roughly and he got so in the habit of saying it that he started saying it when he was asking for my details.

65
00:03:46,996 --> 00:03:50,542
He's like roughly what's your phone number?

66
00:03:50,542 --> 00:03:54,328
I'm like if you want a ballpark.

67
00:03:54,328 --> 00:04:03,557
It's about half a billion.

68
00:04:03,557 --> 00:04:06,227
Coffee is too strong.

69
00:04:06,227 --> 00:04:10,016
This stuff it's too, it's too strong.

70
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:13,802
You know I mean I remember back in the day coffee used to be nice.

71
00:04:13,802 --> 00:04:17,077
You could drink coffee in the morning and go to sleep the same night.

72
00:04:17,077 --> 00:04:20,635
Like you could even drink it at night time.

73
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:23,733
Like you could whip up a blend 43.

74
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:29,909
Watch a couple of episodes and then sink into the night, you know.

75
00:04:29,909 --> 00:04:34,816
Nowadays I have a sip of coffee and I get anxiety. And diarrhea.

76
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:38,895
I see my barista and my guts flinch.

77
00:04:38,895 --> 00:04:42,912
Having a panic attack in the coffee store. I don't know.

78
00:04:42,912 --> 00:04:47,329
There's no drink that's as relaxing as coffee gets you g'd up.

79
00:04:47,329 --> 00:04:50,044
Someone's trying to tell me that was chamomile tea.

80
00:04:50,044 --> 00:04:52,063
But chamomile tea sucks.

81
00:04:52,063 --> 00:05:00,609
Chamomile tea tastes like if water got wet.

82
00:05:00,609 --> 00:05:03,000
Maybe I'm being harsh.

83
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,771
I like, I like the scent of it.

84
00:05:05,771 --> 00:05:09,943
I've been using this new chamomile shampoo.

85
00:05:09,943 --> 00:05:14,786
Relaxing chamomile flavour.

86
00:05:14,786 --> 00:05:15,775
It's good stuff.

87
00:05:15,775 --> 00:05:17,736
I was using it for the first time.

88
00:05:17,736 --> 00:05:19,739
It's going so well.

89
00:05:19,739 --> 00:05:22,653
But then a bit of it got into my eye.

90
00:05:22,653 --> 00:05:24,625
And it stung a lot.

91
00:05:24,625 --> 00:05:32,112
But I was calm throughout the whole thing.

92
00:05:32,112 --> 00:05:35,356
I don't know, I don't understand it.

93
00:05:35,356 --> 00:05:37,983
Because people ask me to meet for a coffee.

94
00:05:37,983 --> 00:05:41,111
They're like, let's go meet for a coffee.

95
00:05:41,111 --> 00:05:42,253
I don't understand that.

96
00:05:42,253 --> 00:05:49,251
Because what I'm hearing is, let's go do a poo-poo.

97
00:05:49,251 --> 00:05:50,351
You know what I mean?

98
00:05:50,351 --> 00:05:52,022
It's a one hour meeting.

99
00:05:52,022 --> 00:05:55,363
We've only got a half an hour of face-to-face time.

100
00:05:55,363 --> 00:06:00,361
We're both painting the toilets for 15 minutes each.

101
00:06:00,361 --> 00:06:05,602
All right, I don't know about that one.

102
00:06:05,602 --> 00:06:10,451
And I was a big, big, foodie during lockdown.

103
00:06:10,451 --> 00:06:12,285
Gained quite a bit of weight.

104
00:06:12,285 --> 00:06:16,051
At the end of lockdown, I had to go to the doctors for something else.

105
00:06:16,051 --> 00:06:18,735
Haemorrhoids.

106
