That was my thought.

252
00:14:06,314 --> 00:14:08,549
I'm 27 years old now.

253
00:14:08,549 --> 00:14:10,843
Like I've already been aged out.

254
00:14:10,843 --> 00:14:13,335
Nowadays I log on to Google Chrome.

255
00:14:13,335 --> 00:14:18,276
It's saying I got 280 compromised passwords.

256
00:14:18,276 --> 00:14:21,589
I'm like, what do you want me to do about it?

257
00:14:21,589 --> 00:14:26,916
I'm not about to change 280 passwords.

258
00:14:26,916 --> 00:14:29,030
I'd rather just change my life.

259
00:14:29,030 --> 00:14:32,233
Like I'll be someone else.

260
00:14:32,233 --> 00:14:33,217
I reckon.

261
00:14:33,217 --> 00:14:36,752
They reckon you got to have a unique password for every website.

262
00:14:36,752 --> 00:14:40,133
I don't even remember my dad's birthday.

263
00:14:40,133 --> 00:14:49,244
And that's my password.

264
00:14:49,244 --> 00:14:54,664
They don't honour passwords anymore either. They don't respect passwords.

265
00:14:54,664 --> 00:14:56,615
I've started to notice that.

266
00:14:56,615 --> 00:14:58,627
That's kind of creeping into society.

267
00:14:58,627 --> 00:15:00,018
This disrespect for passwords.

268
00:15:00,018 --> 00:15:03,063
Because back in the day, you go onto a website.

269
00:15:03,063 --> 00:15:07,684
You type your password in and they'll be like, yeah, we've heard that.

270
00:15:07,684 --> 00:15:08,710
Like we honour that.

271
00:15:08,710 --> 00:15:12,670
Come on in. Explore the possibilities.

272
00:15:12,670 --> 00:15:15,124
They don't honour passwords anymore.

273
00:15:15,124 --> 00:15:20,610
You ever tried logging into your email from someone else's computer?

274
00:15:20,610 --> 00:15:23,697
They don't let you in anymore.

275
00:15:23,697 --> 00:15:25,555
They send you a text.

276
00:15:25,555 --> 00:15:27,377
You got to print that text out.

277
00:15:27,377 --> 00:15:30,703
Get your dad to sign it.

278
00:15:30,703 --> 00:15:34,499
He takes it into the mayor, right?

279
00:15:34,499 --> 00:15:38,331
The mayor shows you nine unique images.

280
00:15:38,331 --> 00:15:41,931
You got to tell him which one's got a street sign in it.

281
00:15:41,931 --> 00:15:44,790
I don't understand the logic behind this.

282
00:15:44,790 --> 00:15:47,936
Because you're telling me, like, a computer hacker.

283
00:15:47,936 --> 00:15:50,157
They've gone to school for three years.

284
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:53,049
But they don't know what a street sign looks like.

285
00:15:53,049 --> 00:15:54,541
Blows my mind.

286
00:15:54,541 --> 00:15:58,437
At the bottom, like the reason it says, prove you're not a robot.

287
00:15:58,437 --> 00:16:02,392
And it's like, I don't know whether or not I am a robot.

288
00:16:02,392 --> 00:16:07,503
But I know for sure that you are a robot.&nbsp; You are a website.

289
00:16:07,503 --> 00:16:09,605
So what's it to you?

290
00:16:09,605 --> 00:16:13,342
What's this self-hating robot doing guarding this page?

291
00:16:13,342 --> 00:16:16,124
If anything, you should be letting me in.

292
00:16:16,124 --> 00:16:18,482
You should say, prove you are a robot.

293
00:16:18,482 --> 00:16:21,830
It didn't affect me too much, this whole passwords thing.

294
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:26,638
Until I was living in this share house and it was in a reception dead zone.

295
00:16:26,638 --> 00:16:29,011
You couldn't get any bars of reception in the house.

296
00:16:29,011 --> 00:16:34,718
And what that means was that I couldn't log in to the email, I couldn't get the texts.

297
00:16:34,718 --> 00:16:35,204
It's a nightmare.

298
00:16:35,204 --> 00:16:37,946
I have to walk out of my house to get reception.

299
00:16:37,946 --> 00:16:42,373
By the time I could get one bar of reception, I was already halfway down the street.

300
00:16:42,373 --> 00:16:44,198
Almost at the post office.

301
00:16:44,198 --> 00:16:49,387
I'm like, I may as well send this email as a letter.

302
00:16:49,387 --> 00:16:54,873
Dear father. Thank you so much for the video.

303
00:16:54,873 --> 00:16:57,145
I'm also suspicious of the vaccine.

304
00:16:57,145 --> 00:17:02,426
I mean, I want to get it taken out of me.

305
00:17:02,426 --> 00:17:06,470
I'm just kidding.

306
00:17:06,470 --> 00:17:13,970
I believe whatever you guys believe.

307
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:16,955
That's good stuff.

308
00:17:16,955 --> 00:17:18,425
I don't know, I'm doing well.

309
00:17:18,425 --> 00:17:27,030
Thanks for asking.

310
00:17:27,030 --> 00:17:32,898
Normally, comedians will wait for like a big laugh or applause break to drink water.

311
00:17:32,898 --> 00:17:42,351
But an opportunity has not yet presented itself.

312
00:17:42,351 --> 00:17:44,851
No, I'm doing good.

